sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Tenant Admin (browser)
    participant API as Platform API (billing module)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL
    participant Stripe as Stripe
    participant Webhook as Webhook Handler (billing)
    participant Notif as notification module

    Admin->>API: POST /api/v1/billing/checkout-session (planId)
    API->>PG: load Tenant, current Subscription (if any)
    API->>Stripe: create Checkout Session (customer, price, tenant_id in metadata)
    Stripe-->>API: session.url
    API-->>Admin: redirect to Stripe-hosted checkout

    Admin->>Stripe: complete payment on Stripe-hosted page
    Stripe-->>Admin: redirect to success_url

    Stripe->>Webhook: POST /api/v1/billing/webhooks (checkout.session.completed)
    Webhook->>Webhook: verify Stripe signature (webhook secret)
    Webhook->>PG: BEGIN, upsert Subscription(status=active, stripe_subscription_id), COMMIT
    Webhook-->>Stripe: 200 OK (ack within timeout)
    Webhook->>Notif: publish "subscription activated" (via outbox/RabbitMQ)
    Notif-->>Admin: email/push "Your Pro plan is active"

    Note over Stripe,Webhook: Later, recurring cycle
    Stripe->>Webhook: POST webhook (invoice.paid)
    Webhook->>PG: update Subscription.current_period_end, record UsageRecord reconciliation
    Stripe->>Webhook: POST webhook (customer.subscription.updated)
    Webhook->>PG: sync status (active/past_due/canceled), update Plan if changed

    Note over Stripe,Webhook: Payment failure → dunning
    Stripe->>Webhook: POST webhook (invoice.payment_failed)
    Webhook->>PG: set Subscription.status = past_due
    Webhook->>Notif: publish "payment failed" reminder
    Note over Webhook: After Stripe's dunning retries exhaust,<br/>subscription.updated (status=canceled) downgrades<br/>tenant to Free-tier entitlements, not immediate lockout.
